# RAGLab local environment for the hard answer harness.
#
# Copy this file to raglab/.env (that exact path - config.py loads raglab/.env, and .gitignore
# already keeps it out of git). Fill in values; never commit the filled copy. Nothing in this repo
# prints a key: the harness masks to the first 8 characters, which is the gateway's own rule.
#
# After editing, check yourself with:  python hard_harness_main.py doctor
# That command spends nothing - it lists models per key and reports which one the current plan
# phase still needs.


### Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Embeddings for retrieval and the LLM-free retrieval judge (nvidia/nemotron-3-embed-1b).
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# The answer model. Answering is xKiro's qwen/qwen3.8-max:free and nothing else; the harness
# refuses other SKUs rather than substituting one.
XKIRO_API_KEY=

# The judging role. This one is NOT a free tier: routed tokens are billed per token against your
# account credits, and the plan has to say grader_llm.credits_acknowledged=true or the harness
# stops. Roughly 46 requests for 300 comparisons at ~10k tokens each.
EXPERIENTIAL_API_KEY=


### Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# A second xKiro key. CI uses it for the authoring role; locally you only need it if you run the
# author phase too.
XKIRO_API_KEY_JINKO=

# Reference-side authoring/auditing (the plan's `llm` role). Skipped by grading and answering.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Point the judging adapter at another deployment of the same gateway. Only an OpenAI-compatible
# Experiential Labs base URL is accepted; nothing here may redirect to a different vendor.
#EXPERIENTIAL_BASE_URL=https://api.experientiallabs.ai/v1

# Which named credential the harness should read, with its value in HARNESS_API_KEY. This is how CI
# injects one secret without naming it in the workflow; you normally set the keys above instead.
#HARNESS_CREDENTIAL_ALIAS=XKIRO_API_KEY
#HARNESS_API_KEY=

# Chunking is pinned in raglab/benchmarks/hard_harness_plan.json (currently 640/40), NOT here, so a
# stray shell value cannot silently change the frozen dataset version. CHUNK_SIZE_TOKENS here only
# affects the main application, which still defaults to 220.
#CHUNK_SIZE_TOKENS=640
#CHUNK_OVERLAP_TOKENS=40

# Retrieval judge: 100 families per language by default (300 questions). 0 judges every accepted
# family. Full pool and sampled numbers are different measurements and are not comparable.
#HARD_HARNESS_JUDGE_LIMIT_PER_LANGUAGE=100

# Where tiktoken keeps cl100k_base. Without it the chunker falls back to a chars/4 estimator,
# chunk boundaries move, and your recall numbers stop meaning the same thing as CI's. The doctor
# step warns loudly about this.
#TIKTOKEN_CACHE_DIR=.cache/hard_harness/tokenizer

# Where embeddings are cached, so a re-run costs no calls. The file is resumable; delete it only if
# you want to re-measure the index from scratch.
#NVIDIA_EMBEDDING_CACHE_FILE=.cache/hard_harness/embeddings_cache_nvidia.json

# Per-job soft deadline in minutes (CI uses 105 for grading).
#HARNESS_DEADLINE_MINUTES=105


### Deliberately absent ----------------------------------------------------

# EMBEDDING_MODEL, ANSWER_MODEL and the translation knobs are not here on purpose: config.py
# rejects stale .env values for them instead of using them. Model selection lives in code and in
# the plan file, so a local override can never quietly change what a published number means.
